WEBVTT

NOTE
The narration of the Atlas walkthrough film (atlas-walkthrough.mp4), as
captions. They sit at the top of the picture (line:5%), so they never
cover the film's own caption bar at its foot. The words, with the times
they are spoken, are the narration script.

00:00:00.461 --> 00:00:03.340 line:5%
Chernozem Atlas: how an office uses it.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.457 line:5%
The totals for cropland,
black soil, damage and people.

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:12.657 line:5%
Where to start: the map,
coloured by priority, and the top areas below.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.830 line:5%
Pick any analysed month.
The Atlas runs again every month, by itself.

00:00:19.426 --> 00:00:24.726 line:5%
Switch between near term and post-crisis:
two ways to rank the same land.

00:00:25.407 --> 00:00:30.397 line:5%
Next steps are worked out from the data.
Tick them off as your team goes.

00:00:31.012 --> 00:00:33.165 line:5%
Type a budget to see what it covers.

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:38.075 line:5%
The map shows priority square by square,
with each state's name and border.

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:41.165 line:5%
The darker the green, the higher the priority.

00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:47.813 line:5%
Colour the map by value, by damage,
by feasibility, or all three together.

00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:54.708 line:5%
Macro ranks whole states.
Micro shows every square.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.630 line:5%
Satellite only shows the land itself,
under the squares.

00:01:04.387 --> 00:01:08.447 line:5%
Move the weights, and the map
and the top areas change at once.

00:01:09.612 --> 00:01:15.342 line:5%
The feasibility cutoff leaves out the hardest
land to reach, for now, with a soft edge.

00:01:16.985 --> 00:01:19.938 line:5%
A place's scores, soil, and cost.

00:01:20.238 --> 00:01:25.148 line:5%
Data shows every analysed month.
Hover over a bar for its numbers.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:34.075 line:5%
Switch between heavily damaged land,
new damage, and people, month by month.

00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:38.565 line:5%
Compare two months: what changed,
and the squares that changed most.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.905 line:5%
The report puts it on one page:

00:01:40.955 --> 00:01:45.765 line:5%
the totals, the top ten places,
the settings, and this month's alerts.

00:01:52.002 --> 00:01:54.319 line:5%
Save it as a PDF for donors.

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:59.739 line:5%
Ask the assistant about any place.
It answers from the same numbers as the map.

00:02:02.771 --> 00:02:06.541 line:5%
Here is a saved conversation
about one of the top areas.

00:02:07.592 --> 00:02:11.932 line:5%
Settings holds the areas,
the crisis, the data, and the team.

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:21.549 line:5%
To add a new area, choose a country or region,
type GPS coordinates, or draw a shape.

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:23.299 line:5%
Here, Moldova.

00:02:27.452 --> 00:02:32.272 line:5%
The last twelve months are analysed,
and the area joins the list and the map.

00:02:37.406 --> 00:02:41.066 line:5%
The team: who can see this area,
and who can change it.

00:02:41.652 --> 00:02:43.732 line:5%
And the crisis, if there is one.

00:02:44.439 --> 00:02:47.800 line:5%
Register at chernozem.app
and rank your own region.
